I’ll inspect the measurement metadata and pattern first, then identify candidate phases, build a multiphase GSAS-II refinement, and verify that every submitted artifact is generated from the saved final project. I’ll keep phase identification and fraction uncertainty explicit where the data do not support a unique answer.

The chemistry strongly suggests cobalt tungstate formation, but at 500 °C residual Co₃O₄ and/or WO₃ are plausible, so I won’t assume a single phase. I’m now extracting peak positions and searching the local crystallographic database for Co–W–O structures and precursor polymorphs before committing to a refinement model.

Peak matching identifies two crystalline phases: monoclinic WO₃ and spinel Co₃O₄. The diagnostic CoWO₄ (111) reflection near 30.6° is absent, while the full Co₃O₄ sequence (about 19.4, 31.6, 37.2, 45.1, 59.7, and 65.6°) is present. The common angle-dependent offset is consistent with reflection-geometry specimen displacement, which I’ll model explicitly rather than forcing it into the lattice parameters.

The first full refinement confirms both phases and gives a near-stoichiometric precursor ratio (roughly 74 wt% WO₃ / 26 wt% Co₃O₄). Profile broadening alone already fits well; attempting separate crystallite-size and microstrain terms makes them singular against the uncalibrated instrumental profile, so those quantities are not independently supportable and will be omitted from the final model.

The final refinement is now in its covariance-stabilization pass: the strongly correlated Caglioti profile term has been fixed after fitting, while phase scales and cells remain refined. This changes the crystalline fractions by less than 0.01 wt% and removes the profile singularity without materially changing the fit.

The refinement is complete and stable: monoclinic WO₃ is 71.49 wt% and spinel Co₃O₄ is 28.51 wt% of the modeled crystalline material. The final Rwp is 3.414% (GOF 1.982), and the submitted atomic models retain reference coordinates while refining the lattice parameters; the data do not justify independent oxygen-coordinate, size, or microstrain refinement.

Completed the GSAS-II refinement.

- Monoclinic WO₃: 71.49 wt%
- Spinel Co₃O₄: 28.51 wt%
- Rwp: 3.414%; Rp: 2.427%; GOF: 1.982
- No detectable crystalline CoWO₄

